{
  // `src/` alone, with no platform surface at all: `lib` is ES2024 and `types`
  // is empty, exactly as packages/domain does it. **This is the program that
  // enforces the boundary**, and it is the reason the wider one above is
  // allowed to admit the DOM.
  //
  // The whole point of #39 is that the same interfaces are satisfied, unchanged,
  // by Web Bluetooth (#40), by CoreBluetooth and the Android BLE APIs (#15) and
  // by the simulator (#44). An interface that can name a browser type has
  // already chosen one of the three — so in this program `navigator`,
  // `BluetoothDevice`, `BluetoothRemoteGATTCharacteristic` and even `DataView`'s
  // GATT-shaped uses are compile errors rather than review findings, and with
  // `types: []` so are `process` and `Buffer`.
  //
  // CLAUDE.md section 4d: that closure is conditional on nothing in the program
  // pulling a `/// <reference types="node" />` back in through a `.d.ts`.
  // `vitest.config.ts` is deliberately excluded here and imports nothing, for
  // the reason its own header records at length.
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "lib": ["ES2024"],
    "types": []
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts"]
}
